WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:07.219
Today is October 04, 2026.

3
00:00:07.219 --> 00:00:15.111
Overnight, benchmark equity indices held near record highs, even as sovereign debt markets flashed historic stress signals.

4
00:00:15.111 --> 00:00:22.464
The Standard and Poor's 500 and the Nasdaq Composite stayed resilient, while the Dow slipped amid industrial weakness.

5
00:00:22.464 --> 00:00:26.091
The primary macro shock remains fixed income.

6
00:00:26.091 --> 00:00:31.741
The ten-year Treasury yield surged to five point three percent, hitting a twenty-year peak.

7
00:00:31.741 --> 00:00:38.481
The thirty-year yield extended to five point six percent, reflecting sustained institutional bond dumping.

8
00:00:38.481 --> 00:00:45.380
Historically, a one-hundred-basis-point surge in yields crunches equity multiples by roughly seven percent.

9
00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:52.623
Over the past twelve months, the S and P forward price-to-earnings multiple compressed from twenty-three down to nineteen.

10
00:00:52.623 --> 00:00:58.738
That eighteen percent multiple contraction absorbed the rate shock without triggering an equity collapse.

11
00:00:58.738 --> 00:01:03.530
The macro debate centers on whether corporate earnings can outrun interest rates.

12
00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:10.074
Bears warn higher debt servicing costs will trigger a lagged earnings contraction across cyclical sectors.

13
00:01:10.074 --> 00:01:18.150
Utilities dropped thirteen percent, real estate fell nearly nine percent, and industrials retreated over five percent this quarter.

14
00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:26.618
Yet bulls point to 1994, when soaring bond yields flattened multiples but thirty-seven percent earnings growth saved equities.

15
00:01:26.618 --> 00:01:33.750
S and P third-quarter earnings growth is currently tracking at twenty-nine percent, defying tightening credit conditions.

16
00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:38.248
Geopolitical fractures are compounding global macro uncertainty.

17
00:01:38.248 --> 00:01:45.258
Middle Eastern escalation threatens critical Saudi energy infrastructure and accelerates non-dollar trade settlements.

18
00:01:45.258 --> 00:01:51.005
In Eastern Europe, tensions around Kaliningrad keep Baltic defense premiums elevated.

19
00:01:51.005 --> 00:01:58.726
In Western Europe, French sovereign debt reached one hundred nineteen percent of GDP, tightening continental fiscal room.

20
00:01:58.726 --> 00:02:05.025
These cross-border liquidity strains have pushed mega-cap technology balance sheets into sharp focus.

21
00:02:05.025 --> 00:02:12.353
Big tech issued two hundred twenty billion dollars in debt this year, yet operational cash flow matches capital spending.

22
00:02:12.353 --> 00:02:21.165
Hyperscalers are directing over eight hundred billion dollars toward artificial intelligence infrastructure, expanding to one point three trillion next year.

23
00:02:21.165 --> 00:02:28.689
Data center capital investments are yielding annualized returns near thirty percent for cloud titans like Amazon and Alphabet.

24
00:02:28.689 --> 00:02:36.434
OpenAI annualized recurring revenue is approaching seventy billion dollars, while Anthropic tracks toward one hundred billion.

25
00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:44.743
Enterprise software budgets continue cutting legacy spending to protect AI deployment, insulating high-performance silicon from rate hikes.

26
00:02:44.743 --> 00:02:52.917
Turning to our pivotal equity focus, Nvidia, ticker N-V-D-A, remains the core pillar of semiconductor capital expenditure.

27
00:02:52.917 --> 00:03:01.961
Despite elevated bond yields, forward order books for accelerated compute platforms remain entirely sold out across tier-one cloud providers.

28
00:03:01.961 --> 00:03:08.726
Institutions are treating current rate volatility as a tactical consolidation rather than structural distribution.

29
00:03:08.726 --> 00:03:15.209
On the technical chart, Nvidia faces heavy overhead resistance near one hundred thirty-five dollars.

30
00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:20.466
Immediate institutional bid support sits firmly at one hundred fifteen dollars.

31
00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:26.496
A breach below one hundred ten dollars represents our key risk boundary to trim beta exposure.

32
00:03:26.496 --> 00:03:35.233
Next, Tesla, ticker T-S-L-A, faces divergent pressures between automotive financing rates and autonomous compute investments.

33
00:03:35.233 --> 00:03:41.667
High interest rates continue pressuring consumer auto loan affordability and automotive gross margins.

34
00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:48.971
However, institutional buyers are closely watching autonomy milestones and dedicated hardware cluster rollouts.

35
00:03:48.971 --> 00:03:57.121
Tesla holds major technical resistance around two hundred sixty dollars, with pivotal volume support resting at two hundred ten dollars.

36
00:03:57.121 --> 00:04:03.714
Sustained price action below one hundred ninety-five dollars signals severe caution for momentum traders.

37
00:04:03.848 --> 00:04:11.886
Finally, Apple, ticker A-A-P-L, serves as a high-margin cash defensive play amidst sovereign debt volatility.

38
00:04:11.836 --> 00:04:19.569
Strong enterprise hardware refresh cycles and resilient services revenue provide reliable buffer against macro headwinds.

39
00:04:19.569 --> 00:04:27.154
Technical resistance sits at two hundred thirty-two dollars, with foundational floor support anchored at two hundred eighteen dollars.

40
00:04:27.154 --> 00:04:31.162
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

41
00:04:31.162 --> 00:04:35.328
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
